<title>POLAND: POLISH KPW CLEARS ENERGOAPARATURA ISSUE FOR TRADE.</title>
<headline>POLISH KPW CLEARS ENERGOAPARATURA ISSUE FOR TRADE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Securities Commission</p>
<p>(KPW) has cleared for public trade an issue by engineering firm</p>
<p>Energoaparatura SA to selected investors, the KPW said in a</p>
<p>statement on Thursday.</p>
<p> Tranches		  No Of Shares	   Subscription</p>
<p>			     Offered		  Period</p>
<p>Polish American</p>
<p> Enterprise Fund	 95,382		   Sept 15-18</p>
<p>Polish Private</p>
<p> Equity Fund I	   107,687		  Sept 15-18</p>
<p>Polish Private</p>
<p> Equity Fund II	  104,617		  Sept 15-18</p>
<p> PBR			  79,920		  Sept 15-18</p>
<p> Lead Manager:	   PBR SA brokerage</p>
<p>Use Of Proceeds: purchase of new equipment and machinery</p>
<p>The company seeks a listing on the Warsaw bourse's third</p>
<p>so-called free market later this month.</p>
<p>EARNINGS DATA</p>
<p>			    1996		     1995</p>
<p>(in mln of PLN)</p>
<p> Net profit:	    2.50		     1.84</p>
<p> Sales:		  62.08		    41.15</p>
<p>Main Shareholders:</p>
<p>Polish American Enterprise Fund - 14.8 pct of shares</p>
<p> Polish Private Equity Fund I    - 16.7 pct of shares</p>
<p> Polish private Equity Fund II   - 16.2  pct of shares</p>
<p> PBR		     - 11.9 pct of shares</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
